# Frontend — components & performance

Design will change often. Build **replaceable pieces**, not page monoliths.

## Atomic layout (small → large)

| Level | Where | Examples |
|-------|--------|----------|
| **Primitives** | `components/ui/` | Button, Input, Avatar, Icon |
| **Composites** | `components/` or `components/blocks/` | AuthForm, WorkCard, DirectionChips |
| **Features** | `components/<feature>/` or route `_components/` | ProfileEditor, WorksFeed |
| **Pages** | `app/[locale]/...` | Compose only — almost no markup logic |

Promote to `components/ui/` only when used in **2+** places or clearly a design-system atom.

## Rules

- **One component, one job** — presentational vs container/hooks split when state grows
- **Props in, events out** — unidirectional data; no child→parent mutation of shared objects
- **No hardcoded UI copy** — next-intl only (see i18n rule)
- **Composable API** — prefer `children` / slots over mega-prop configs
- **Stable public props** — rename internals freely; avoid breaking callers during redesigns
- **Colocate** — styles/hooks next to the component; shared hooks in `lib/` or `hooks/`

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — 400-line page with inline buttons and fetch
// ✅ GOOD — <WorksFeed /> uses <WorkCard /> + <DirectionChips />; page only layouts
```

## Data & rendering

- **Auth/session reads in RSC** — load `me` / profile via server loaders (`lib/session.ts`); forward cookies with `createServerApiClient` (`API_INTERNAL_URL` in Docker). Client components own mutations only (`logout`, PATCH, upload) + `router.refresh()` when RSC data must update
- Do not `useEffect`+fetch for initial auth state the server already knows from cookies
- Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default — only for proven expensive trees or stable deps
- Lists: stable `key`s (ids, not indexes); virtualize only when lists are huge
- Images: sized, lazy below fold; avoid layout shift
- Prefer CSS/`next/font` over JS animation libraries unless motion is a product requirement
- Avoid prop-drilling through 4+ levels — lift state or pass a narrow context

## Redesign-friendly

- Visual tokens (colors, spacing, type) via Tailwind theme / CSS variables — not scattered hex in JSX
- Do not couple business labels to CSS class names
- Swapping a primitive (e.g. new Button) must not require rewriting features
